Self, played by Ushio Shinohara.

6
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Cutie and the Boxer is a 2013 American documentary film
produced, shot, and directed by Zachary Heinzerling.

7
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:21,000
The film focuses on the chaotic 40-year marriage of two artists, Noriko Shinohara and her
husband the boxing painter Ushio, featuring original artwork by the couple.

8
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Heinzerling said of the couple:  "When I first met [the Shinoharas], I was just struck by the raw spirit and beauty that
emanates from their faces, their lifestyle, their art, everything about them has so much purpose and character.

9
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:51,000
Even if you don’t speak Japanese, even if you have no previous knowledge of their
artwork or who they are, you’re immediately captivated by their presence.

10
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
They live in a world that’s kind of a time warp that hearkens back to the ‘70s New York SoHo art
scene that is sort of canonized in history, certainly from my point of view."

11
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
The film explores themes of artist, painter, art, elderly.
